      "markdown": "# Code panel prototype\n\nOpen **Code**, next to Scenes and Math. The upper area is a folder browser; selecting a file opens it below without moving the lesson. Widen the left dock by dragging its edge.\n\nClick a line number or select part of an expression. **Ask AI** and **Go to step** appear together below the code. A line used more than once offers a choice of lesson steps. Nothing jumps merely because you selected it.\n\nThe gold left border indicates the current execution position; the thin selection outline is your independent reading selection. Blue, gold and green spans demonstrate authored expression marks.\n\n## Variables\n\n**text** is the input character sequence `([])`. **i** is the next/current reading position. **stack** contains input indices of unmatched opening characters, bottom to top. **ch** is the current character read by the displayed loop.\n\nThe code is never executed. Six complete lesson snapshots supply values to the ordinary expression bindings. Use the **state player** below the scene to inspect them directly. Lesson sections and execution states are separate.\n\nThis small prototype demonstrates panel interaction and bindings. Free-form input editing, full code syntax coloring and a dedicated stack renderer are outside this slice.",
